th)", "All nine expert raters place the race at Safe/Solid or Likely R", "Polymarket prices Smith's chances at just 10%"], "rationale": "The R+7 lean, Allen's incumbency and overwhelming fundraising edge, and a unanimous expert consensus of Safe-to-Likely R all point to a comfortable Republican win, with markets pricing Smith near 10%. The forecast lands near the rating-implied margin, slightly beyond the fundamentals-only estimate given the lopsided money gap.", "watch": "A major national Democratic wave environment or an unexpected Allen scandal could pull the race toward Lean R territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Rick Allen (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican incumbent Rick Allen seeks another term in Georgia's 12th District, a seat with a Republican partisan lean of about seven points. He cleared his primary in May and enters the general election with roughly $1.3 million on hand, while Democratic nominee Ceretta Smith, a local lawmaker who won a June runoff, has raised under $27,000 and holds only about $3,500. No outside spending has been reported on either side.\n\nEvery major race rater calls the district Safe or Solid Republican, with two rating it merely Likely R, and prediction markets give Smith about a one-in-ten chance. With no public polling available, the race rests on fundamentals, and those fundamentals point clearly toward Allen's reelection.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0633, "margin": -10.05}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0456, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0466, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0433, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0323, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0215, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0217, "margin": -13.0}]}